 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/Abelian.lean:247-276 gives the equivalence plus its coercion lemmas; TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Basic.lean:154-172 rebuilds the injection by hand. `Module.Finite.equiv` is the idiom already used at TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Schur.lean:193.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Delete both private declarations and prove `instFiniteDimensional` as `Module.Finite.equiv (LieModule.maxTrivLinearMapEquivLieModuleHom (R := K) (L := L) (M := M) (N := N))`, a submodule of the finite-dimensional `M \u2192\u2097[K] N`. This needs `[LieModule K L M]` added to the instance, since `LinearMap.instLieRingModule` (mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/Basic.lean:248) sits under the section variables `[LieModule R L M] [LieModule R L N]` (:140-141); that hypothesis is available at the only in-repo use site, `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Schur.lean:192`.",
   "issue": "The private `LieModuleHom.toLinearMap\u2097` (:154) and `toLinearMap\u2097_injective` (:159) re-derive the embedding of `M \u2192\u2097\u2045K,L\u2046 N` into `M \u2192\u2097[K] N` that Mathlib already provides as the `R`-linear equivalence `LieModule.maxTrivLinearMapEquivLieModuleHom : maxTrivSubmodule R L (M \u2192\u2097[R] N) \u2243\u2097[R] M \u2192\u2097\u2045R,L\u2046 N` (mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Lie/Abelian.lean:247), which is unused anywhere in TauCeti (`grep maxTrivLinearMapEquivLieModuleHom code/TauCeti` \u2192 no hits).",
   "line": "154"
  }
 ],
